# 13D.3 Add a current relationship method to SQLiteStore

Add this method to `SQLiteStore`:

```python
def current_relationships(self):
    cursor = self.conn.execute(
        """
        SELECT
            r.source_entity_type,
            r.source_entity_id,
            r.relationship_type,
            r.target_entity_type,
            r.target_entity_id,
            r.timestamp
        FROM relationships r
        INNER JOIN (
            SELECT
                source_entity_type,
                source_entity_id,
                relationship_type,
                target_entity_type,
                target_entity_id,
                MAX(timestamp) AS latest_timestamp
            FROM relationships
            GROUP BY
                source_entity_type,
                source_entity_id,
                relationship_type,
                target_entity_type,
                target_entity_id
        ) latest
        ON r.source_entity_type = latest.source_entity_type
        AND r.source_entity_id = latest.source_entity_id
        AND r.relationship_type = latest.relationship_type
        AND r.target_entity_type = latest.target_entity_type
        AND r.target_entity_id = latest.target_entity_id
        AND r.timestamp = latest.latest_timestamp
        ORDER BY r.id ASC
        """
    )

    return cursor.fetchall()
```

### What does this do?

Suppose your database contains:

```text
