# 13D.6 One improvement: don't rely on dictionary insertion semantics

I'd actually recommend making it explicit:

```python
def current_relationships(self):

    relationships = self.all_relationships()

    latest = {}

    for relationship in relationships:

        key = (
            relationship[0],  # source type
            relationship[1],  # source id
            relationship[2],  # relationship type
        )

        existing = latest.get(key)

        if existing is None:
            latest[key] = relationship
            continue

        if relationship[5] > existing[5]:
            latest[key] = relationship

    return list(latest.values())
```

This says exactly what we mean:

> For every source + relationship type, keep the newest relationship.

